# FreeType 2.10.0 — our delta from pristine upstream.
#
# Upstream: https://download.savannah.gnu.org/releases/freetype/freetype-2.10.0.tar.gz
#           sha256 955e17244e9b38adb0c98df66abb50467312e6bb70eac07e49ce6bd1a20e809a
# Apply from sdk/lib/3rdparty/freetype/ with: patch -p1 < vendor-patches/freetype.patch
#
# 449 files exist in both trees; 432 are byte-identical. SIXTEEN differ, and every one of
# them is wrapped in #ifdef __REACTOS__ / #ifndef __REACTOS__ — so undefining that macro
# gives you pristine upstream behaviour. There is no unmarked edit anywhere in the tree.
# (A seventeenth file, include/freetype/internal/ftdebug.h, differed by a single added
# blank line and was reverted to pristine on 2026-09-20 rather than carried.)
# Not vendored, by design: builds/, devel/, docs/, objs/ and the per-directory
# Jamfile/module.mk/rules.mk build chaff — 81 files, all build system. TechNote.txt in
# the tree says to delete exactly those.
#
# TWO THEMES COVER FOURTEEN OF THE SIXTEEN:
#
#   STACK -> HEAP (the big one). TechNote.txt: "Stack size is limited, so we have to use
#   malloc/free instead of large stack variables." Pattern is mechanical:
#   `FooRec worker[1];` becomes `FooRec *worker = malloc(sizeof(*worker));` with a null
#   check and free() on every exit path. Files: sfnt/ttsbit.c, raster/ftraster.c,
#   psaux/psintrp.c, cid/cidgload.c, type1/t1gload.c, smooth/ftgrays.c,
#   autofit/{aflatin,aflatin2,afcjk,afmodule}.c. This changes WHERE a fixed-size struct
#   lives, not its size — no bounds, length or offset arithmetic is touched.
#
#   *** A REAL BUG LIVES IN THIS SET, currently unreachable ***
#   autofit/aflatin2.c has
#         AF_LatinMetricsRec *dummy = malloc(sizeof(*dummy));
#         if (dummy) goto Exit;
#   The test is INVERTED. The identical construct in the sibling files afcjk.c and
#   aflatin.c correctly reads `if (!dummy) goto Exit;`. As written, the success path
#   skips the whole width-computation block and silently falls back to a constant width.
#   It is dead today: every caller is behind #ifdef FT_OPTION_AUTOFIT2, which is
#   referenced in five places and DEFINED IN NONE (verified by grep across the tree and
#   the CMakeLists). So: real defect, zero runtime effect, one-line fix whenever someone
#   is next in there. Left alone here because this pass records state, it does not patch
#   logic.
#
#   CONFIG / GLUE. ftoption.h flips three macros under __REACTOS__ (disables
#   ENVIRONMENT_PROPERTIES, enables SUBPIXEL_RENDERING, enables DEBUG_LEVEL_ERROR only in
#   checked builds) — these three ARE pure toggles and are the one cluster here that could
#   move into the build as -D flags. base/ftdebug.c wraps FT_Message/FT_Panic in
#   #ifndef __REACTOS__ because the win32k font driver glue supplies its own.
#   base/ftlcdfil.c changes one parameter from FT_Vector* to FT_Vector[3].
#
# TWO DELIBERATE FEATURES, not mechanical:
#   ftbitmap.h + base/ftbitmap.c   add FT_Bitmap_Convert_ReactOS_Hack(), an extended
#       FT_Bitmap_Convert that can emit 0xFF/0x00 bytes rather than 1/0 bits for text
#       output; the original name survives as a wrapper passing hack=FALSE, so upstream
#       behaviour is unchanged. Named explicitly in TechNote.txt.
#   sfnt/ttcmap.c                  adds a DEFENSIVE check in tt_cmap4_char_map_binary:
#       reads the subtable's format field and refuses to parse unless it is 4, citing
#       ReactOS bug CORE-12549 (stale cmap data after a font file is replaced on disk).
#       This HARDENS the parser; it does not relax it.
#
# SECURITY: FreeType parses untrusted fonts, so note what is NOT here. No bounds check,
# allocation size, or length/offset arithmetic differs from upstream anywhere in the
# sixteen files. No backported CVE fix is present either — this is stock 2.10.0 (2019-03)
# and roughly a dozen CVEs behind, which is the standing item in `staleness:`.
# FT_CONFIG_OPTION_USE_PNG is NOT enabled (ftoption.h:281 still has it commented out and
# the CMakeLists never -D's it), so sfnt/pngshim.c compiles to `typedef int
# _pngshim_dummy;` and CVE-2020-15999 — the sbix embedded-PNG heap overflow exploited as
# a Chrome 0-day — is NOT REACHABLE HERE. Verified in the tree twice, independently.
#
# No copyright line or licence header differs anywhere in the delta.
#
